# What stays on this machine, and what ships.
#
# This directory is both the source checkout and the runtime install, so the two
# kinds of file sit side by side: everything tracked is the product, everything
# below is yours. The distinction is load-bearing in three ways — a credential
# must never reach history, `make release` builds only from tracked files, and a
# worktree-sweeping tool reads an unignored stray as an edit to move aside.
#
# That last one is not hypothetical. v1.4.0 renamed `model-registry.conf` to
# `model-registry`; the `*.conf` rule had been the only thing keeping it out of
# git, so the new name was ignored by nothing, a reconcile read it as a stray,
# and 52 probed context windows went to a quarantine branch. The rule landed
# nine minutes after the loss.
#
# So: a state file's name and its ignore rule are one fact.
# `test_every_state_file_is_gitignored` asserts they agree, in both directions —
# state must be ignored, shipped components must not be. Add a rule here and add
# the path there, or the test is the thing that fails instead of your data.

# ── Credentials ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# One profile per file, holding an API key, an OAuth token, or an account email.
# Mode 0600, created by `ccmorph add`, never tracked in this repository's
# history — verified by `git log --all --diff-filter=A`.
*.conf
# Per-profile system prompts: profile-local, and prompts can quote private work.
*.system.md

# ── Machine-local state ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Probed context ceilings, written by `ccmorph probe`. Machine-local because
# a ceiling is a property of the ROUTE this host takes to a gateway; another
# host's registry is wrong here, sometimes dangerously (too high means a session
# dies mid-conversation instead of compacting).
model-registry
# Sidecar lock serializing concurrent registry writes (refresh-model-registry).
model-registry.lock
# Single-profile context writes and migration coordination contain no configuration.
*.conf.lock
.context-migration.lock
.profile-home-migration.lock
# Recoverable legacy context sources, never active configuration.
model-registry*.migrated*
# Which profile a bare `claude` uses.
active
# Mid-session relay handoff: written by `ccrelay`, consumed by the next launch.
.reswitch.*
# Host opt-ins, sourced by ccmorph.sh at load. Trusted executable zsh, and the
# one seam where a machine's own tooling turns on behaviour the product knows
# nothing about — so by construction it is never shippable.
local.sh

# ── Runtime output ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Rotated in place by _ccm_log. Diagnostics, not state: safe to delete.
ccmorph.log
# Snapshots taken before a risky edit, and profile dirs left behind by a deleted
# conf. Both hold credential-shaped content, so they are ignored rather than
# tidied away by hand.
backups/
orphaned-profiles/
# Provider OAuth credentials (cliproxyapi auth dirs, one per provider profile).
# Never committable — this is the whole reason auth/ has its own 0700 root.
auth/
# Claude-compatible per-profile runtime homes, including private authentication.
profiles/
# Hand-made copies of the runtime, from before a risky change. Two exist on the
# author's machine and one is mode 0600; a narrower `ccmorph.sh.bak-*` rule left
# every other spelling exposed, so match the suffix wherever it lands. Verified by
# swapping this file in and watching both reappear as untracked.
*.bak
*.bak-*
*.orig
*.rej
*.sync-bak

# ── Build and test artifacts ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Release tarballs from `make release`. Built by `git archive` at a tag, so they
# are reproducible from history and never worth keeping.
dist/
# Python bytecode and pytest state.
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/

# ── Agent and editor scratch ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The project skill under .claude/skills ships; a global `.claude/` ignore must
# not hide it. Only the machine-local entries below stay out.
!.claude/
# Claude Code session worktrees: lanes live here and are reaped after promotion.
.claude/worktrees/
# Scheduled-task lockfile, per-machine.
.claude/scheduled_tasks.lock
# Background task receipts and logs are local verification evidence, not product.
.pi/tasks/
# .git-worktree-policy is committed integration intent, not machine-local state.
# Editor and OS droppings, ignored so they cannot become an accidental commit in
# a directory where `git add -A` is one keystroke from a credential.
.officecli/
.DS_Store
*.swp
*~
.impeccable/hook.cache.json

# ccmorph-rc-hosts folder list: machine-local (paths, route choice)
rc-hosts

# ccmorph-rc: the folder's kept Remote Control host
.claude/rc-host.json
